{%- set order = ["workflow", "org", "governance", "context"] -%}

<section class="m-sec">
  <div class="m-hero">
    <div class="m-hero-copy">
      <span class="m-eyebrow">AI transformation, from the inside</span>
      <h1>AI makes people faster. Is it making your organisation faster?</h1>
      <p class="m-lede">AI accelerates individual tasks, but better tools alone don’t make organisations more productive. That requires rethinking how work flows, teams collaborate and leaders make decisions.</p>
      <p class="m-lede">This site is what I’ve learned redesigning all three from the inside.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="m-iso-wrap">
      <div class="m-iso" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="m-plane p-context" style="--i:0" data-layer="context" data-href="/context-layer/"></div>
        <div class="m-plane p-workflow" style="--i:1" data-layer="workflow" data-href="/workflow/"><div class="track"><i class="g-ai"></i><i class="g-ai"></i><i class="g-human"></i><i class="g-ai"></i><i class="g-human"></i><i class="g-ai"></i><i class="g-human"></i></div></div>
        <div class="m-plane p-org" style="--i:2" data-layer="org" data-href="/org-design/"><div class="grid">{% for n in range(9) %}<i></i>{% endfor %}</div></div>
        <div class="m-plane p-gov" style="--i:3" data-layer="governance" data-href="/governance/"><div class="bars"><i class="ai" style="width:88%"></i><i style="width:62%"></i><i class="ai" style="width:74%"></i><i style="width:46%"></i><i class="ai" style="width:80%"></i></div></div>
      </div>
      <ul class="m-iso-labels">
        {% for l in layers %}<li><a href="/{{ l.slug }}/" data-layer="{{ l.key }}"><b>{{ l.name }}</b><span>{{ l.sub }}</span></a></li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="m-sec">
  <div class="m-col">
    {% set v = video %}{% set size = "" %}{% include "partials/video.njk" %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="m-sec">
  <h2>What changes when building gets cheap</h2>
  <div class="m-shifts">
    {% for key in order %}{% set l = layers | byKey(key) %}
    <a class="m-shift" href="/{{ l.slug }}/"><span class="ly">{{ l.name }}</span><span class="from">{{ l.shift[0] }}</span><span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="to">{{ l.shift[1] }}</span></a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="m-sec">
  <span class="m-eyebrow">The full story · three minutes</span>
  <h2>Follow one small customer fix through the organisation.</h2>
  <p class="m-lede">It should take a day. Here's where it actually goes, and what I redesigned at each stop.</p>
  <div class="m-walk">
    <div class="m-stop on"><div class="m-rail"><span class="m-dot">1</span></div><div class="m-stopbody">
      <span class="m-req"><i></i>A customer asks for a small fix</span>
      <h3>It arrives under three different names.</h3>
      <p class="m-body">The customer describes what they see on screen. The roadmap knows that area by a codename. The alerts call it a service. An agent reading all three sees three unrelated things.</p>
      <div class="m-names"><span>“the report page”</span><span>roadmap codename</span><span>alerting service</span></div>
      <p class="m-redesign"><b>Context layer:</b> one place that maps names across tools, so the request arrives with its history attached.</p>
      <div class="m-stoplinks"><a class="m-link" href="/context-layer/">The context layer →</a><a class="m-link" href="/essays/the-layer-underneath/">Essay 1 →</a></div>
    </div></div>
    <div class="m-stop"><div class="m-rail"><span class="m-dot">2</span></div><div class="m-stopbody">
      <h3>An agent drafts the fix in hours. Then it waits.</h3>
      <div class="m-mlanes" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="m-mlane"><span>Build</span><span class="bar"><i class="ai" style="width:12%"></i></span></div>
        <div class="m-mlane"><span>Review</span><span class="bar"><i class="wait" style="width:78%"></i></span></div>
        <div class="m-mlane"><span>Ship</span><span class="bar"><i style="width:10%"></i></span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="m-body">Building got cheap. Review didn't. Nearly everything in flight sits waiting for someone to approve it.</p>
      <p class="m-redesign"><b>Workflow:</b> human gates only where there's judgment, and related fixes reviewed together.</p>
      <div class="m-stoplinks"><a class="m-link" href="/workflow/">Workflow →</a></div>
    </div></div>
    <div class="m-stop"><div class="m-rail"><span class="m-dot">3</span></div><div class="m-stopbody">
      <h3>It touches three teams, so it crosses three queues.</h3>
      <div class="m-mchain"><span>Frontend</span><em>wait →</em><span>Backend</span><em>wait →</em><span>Data</span><em>wait →</em><span>QA</span></div>
      <p class="m-body">Each team has its own priorities. The fix is small; the waiting isn't.</p>
      <p class="m-redesign"><b>Org design:</b> small pods that own an outcome end to end, with an agent doing the first cross-domain pass.</p>
      <div class="m-stoplinks"><a class="m-link" href="/org-design/">Org design →</a></div>
    </div></div>
    <div class="m-stop"><div class="m-rail"><span class="m-dot">4</span></div><div class="m-stopbody">
      <h3>The monthly report says it shipped. It hadn't.</h3>
      <div class="m-mreport"><span>Customer fix · status</span><span><s>Shipped</s> · in review</span></div>
      <p class="m-body">Status fields drift. A report assembled from them is confidently wrong, and the team presenting it can't explain why.</p>
      <p class="m-redesign"><b>Governance:</b> an agent drafts the health check, the team corrects it and owns it, and nothing reaches leadership that nobody stands behind.</p>
      <div class="m-stoplinks"><a class="m-link" href="/governance/">Governance →</a></div>
    </div></div>
  </div>
</section>

